&lt;p>&lt;strong>Part 23 of the &lt;em>Learning Quantum Physics&lt;/em> series.&lt;/strong>&lt;/p>
&lt;p>In &lt;a href="https://dasarpai.github.io/dsblog/quantum-computing-careers">Quantum Computing Careers&lt;/a> one layer of the stack is &lt;strong>error correction&lt;/strong>. This article explains that layer.&lt;/p>
&lt;p>Every computer makes mistakes. The questions here are:&lt;/p>
&lt;blockquote>
&lt;p>What is damaged? Why so easily? What can we do without destroying the computation?&lt;/p>&lt;/blockquote></description></item><item><title>Quantum Computing Careers: Where Should a Software Professional Enter — Hardware, Systems, Algorithms, or Applications?</title><link>https://dasarpai.github.io/dsblog/quantum-computing-careers/</link><pubDate>Tue, 15 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>hari@dasarpai.com (Dr. Hari Thapliyaal)</author><guid>https://dasarpai.github.io/dsblog/quantum-computing-careers/</guid><description>&lt;p>
